Drop the trace_printk in the mgmt tx confirm path

Any trace_printk in a module makes the kernel print its "this is a DEBUG
kernel" banner when the module loads. The trace_mgmt_cfm tracepoint right
below records the same confirm when the driver is built with tracepoints.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c	2026-11-12 01:38:24.410541688 +0100
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c	2026-11-12 01:38:24.418863006 +0100
@@ -2391,9 +2391,6 @@
 
     /* Update txq and HW queue credits */
     if (sw_txhdr->desc.host.flags & TXU_CNTRL_MGMT) {
-        trace_printk("done=%d retry_required=%d sw_retry_required=%d acknowledged=%d\n",
-                     rwnx_txst.tx_done, rwnx_txst.retry_required,
-                     rwnx_txst.sw_retry_required, rwnx_txst.acknowledged);
 #ifdef CREATE_TRACE_POINTS
         trace_mgmt_cfm(sw_txhdr->rwnx_vif->vif_index,
                        (sw_txhdr->rwnx_sta) ? sw_txhdr->rwnx_sta->sta_idx : 0xFF,
